{"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"gsroffset":12,"continue":"gsroffset||"},"query":{"pages":{"56240909":{"pageid":56240909,"ns":6,"title":"File:20160604 Azerbaijan 6859 Pano Baku sRGB (31274007253).jpg","index":5,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":3902099,"width":9285,"height":3077,"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/24/20160604_Azerbaijan_6859_Pano_Baku_sRGB_%2831274007253%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20160604_Azerbaijan_6859_Pano_Baku_sRGB_(31274007253).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/56240909","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2017-02-13 14:54:41","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"20160604 Azerbaijan 6859 Pano Baku sRGB (31274007253)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Images with extracted images|Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR|Panoramic photographs of Baku|2016 in Baku|Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"40.357627","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"49.830175","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Panoramic view of Baku from Da\u011f\u00fcst\u00fc Park (with joggers running up the stairs).  On the far left is the General Assembly (Milli Majlis) with its two office towers flanking the meeting chamber in between.  The three glass-sheathed, flame-shaped towers are the Flame Towers which were completed in 2012.  (The Baku coat of arms features three flames representing the natural wealth in oil and gas of the Absheron Peninsula.)  On the right is the Yacht Club in Baku Bay.  The tubular building on shore in front of the Yacht Club is actually shaped like a rolled up carpet to house the new Carpet Museum that opened in 2014.  Along the water\u2019s edge is a park and promenade known as the Bulvar.  The low-rise area adjacent to the waterfront is the Old City.\n</p><p>Baku, the capital and largest city of Azerbaijan, is located on the southern shore of the Absheron Peninsula which juts out from the western coast of the Caspian Sea.  At 28m/92ft below sea level, Baku is the lowest-lying national capital in the world.\n</p><p>The Walled City of Baku with the Shirvanshah's Palace and Maiden Tower became a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2000.\n</p><p>The traditional art of Azerbaijani carpet weaving was inscribed on UNESCO\u2019s Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity in 2010.\n</p><p>On Google Earth:\nDa\u011f\u00fcst\u00fc Park  40\u00b021'26.41\"N, 49\u00b049'45.12\"E \nNational Assembly  40\u00b021'29.34\"N, 49\u00b049'31.85\"E \nFlame Towers  40\u00b021'35.10\"N, 49\u00b049'34.87\"E\nYacht Club  40\u00b021'42.98\"N, 49\u00b050'24.46\"E\n</p>\nOld City  40\u00b021'56.08\"N, 49\u00b050'5.83\"E","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-06-04 10:25","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/9508280@N07/31274007253/\">20160604_Azerbaijan_6859 Pano Baku sRGB</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/9508280@N07\">Dan Lundberg</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-sa-2.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"52120471":{"pageid":52120471,"ns":6,"title":"File:Armenia, Travels and Studies, Vol. 2.djvu","index":12,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":18923370,"width":2273,"height":3628,"pagecount":644,"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Armenia%2C_Travels_and_Studies%2C_Vol._2.djvu?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armenia,_Travels_and_Studies,_Vol._2.djvu","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/52120471","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2016-10-07 19:46:11","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"<div class=\"fn\">\nArmenia, travels and studies</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"1901 books|DjVu files in English|PD-old-100-expired|PD-scan (PD-old-auto-expired)|Scans from the Internet Archive/unverified|CC-PD-Mark|Scans from the Internet Archive|Books without Wikidata item|Armenia Travels and Studies (H. F. B. Lynch)","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:H._F._B._Lynch\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:H. F. B. Lynch\"><span title=\"British traveller, businessman and politician (1862\u20131913)\">H. F. B. Lynch</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Bibliography: v. 2, p. [471]-496","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a href=\"//archive.org/details/armeniatravelsst02lync\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"iarchive:armeniatravelsst02lync\"><bdi class=\"description en\" lang